  m_text: "1. In solids, particles are tightly packed, giving a fixed shape and volume.\n\r\n2.
    In liquids, particles slide past one another\u2014fixed volume but no fixed shape.\n\r\n3.
    In gases, particles are far apart and move freely\u2014no fixed shape or volume.\n\r\n4.
    Heating or cooling changes the speed of particles, leading to changes of state.\r"
